  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"...une imagerie d'apres le conte de Charles Perrault."--Colophon (volumes 1-2, 6)</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Each volume made of accordion-folded sheets (approximately 40 pages) printed one side only and attached continuously with boards at each end; volumes 1-3, 5-6 have cloth-covered boards with title printed on paper label mounted on front cover; volume 4 has paper-covered boards lithographed with handwritten title on front cover and colophon on back cover; volumes housed individually in clear plastic slipcases within publisher's larger color illustrated slipcase.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Les lithographies [sur papier Velin] ... ont été tirées sur les presses des Ateliers Arte, Paris." See special title pages and colophon for volume 4.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">[v. 1]. Le Petit Poucet = Tom Thumb = Däumling  (©1979) -- [v. 2]. Blanche Neige = Snow White = Schneewittchen (©1974) -- [v. 3]. Le Petit Chaperon Rouge = Little Red Riding Hood = Rotkäppchen (©1965) -- [v. 4]. La fable du Hasard = The fable of Hazard = Die Fabel vom Zufall (©1968) -- [v. 5]. La Belle au Bois dormant = Sleeping Beauty = Dornröschen (©1982) -- [v. 6]. Cendrillon = Cinderella = Aschenputtel (©1976).</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Boxed set of conceptual artist's books by Swiss graphic designer and illustrator Warja Lavater collecting her wordless lithographic adaptations of six of Charles Perrault's classic fairy tales, each reimagined visually using ideogramatic color shapes and symbols in place of written language and figural representation.</subfield>
  </datafield>
